    "headline": "FICO Stock Drops the Most in 6 Years. Here’s What Went Wrong.",
    "summary": "FICO dropped on Thursday after the global analytics software company issued lower-than-expected guidance.  The company, formerly known as  Fair Isaac  closed down 17% at $1,139.54, snapping a four-day winning streak to post its largest percent decrease since March 16, 2020, according to Dow Jones Market Data.  For the third quarter of fiscal 2026, the company on Wednesday posted better-than-expected adjusted earnings of $12.18 a share versus consensus expectations for $11.76 a share.",
    "url": "https://www.barrons.com/articles/fico-stock-price-earnings-98f7a635?siteid=yhoof2&yptr=yahoo",
